nal and  they're reasonable and they're about  what kids need to know and not how you  get there yeah that's a great thing and  you know what hasn't said how does that  play out in Arizona and you know how do  you keep it minimal as opposed to okay  well it's good to read and write but  then you also have to have these courses  in place whether or not we test them but  you know to teach citizenship or this  type of hygiene or whatever I think well  I had a superintendent say to me the  other day the biggest problem we've got  in Arizona right now is we're on hiatus  like everybody else we grade our schools  a throughout we use the state tests  right now everybody sort of is an A &amp; B  school so the new test supposed to be  honest and we're gonna get a little more  serious about that but the fact of the  matter is well we don't have a grave the  superintendent was saying look I've had  people in my my office today I'm  supposed to wear a purple shirt because  of domestic violence my kids are  supposed to be in a bullying program  it's football season and the coach wants  this said without that assessment on the  table every year with some consequence a  through F you're gonna get graded he  said these other things just encroach  and I guarantee you everybody loses  focus when parents are or and even kids  are choosing to go to a particular  school will they generate the  information they need in order to make  an informed choice out of consumer  demand because I know if I have my kids  and I can pick from 10 different schools  if the schools are like just trust us  we're you know we're really awesome or  like yeah you know I'm you know that's  going to be hard for me to take but that  will that take the place or will that  supplement kind of these rudimentary  state assessments so we're gonna have  state assessments for a while Nick in an  ideal world the one I'd like to live in  people would be so knowledgeable about  indicators that you wouldn't need one  state 